# CITATION.cff for real-chart-bench
#
# type: dataset — chosen over "software" because the primary citable artifact
# this repository produces is the benchmark dataset (real paper figures paired
# with Starrydata-derived ground-truth XY curves, plus a manifest/registry of
# that data). The evaluation harness (CLI, metrics code) exists to build and
# score that dataset, not the other way around — third parties will mostly
# want to cite "the benchmark dataset we evaluated against," not "the CLI
# tool we ran." CFF permits only one top-level `type`; the harness/code
# aspect is still discoverable via `repository-code` below.
#
# `license` lists both because this repository is deliberately dual-licensed
# by artifact type: the CODE is MIT (owner decision, 2026-09-02 — see LICENSE),
# and the DATA (data/manifest/v0/, data/verified_pairs/, including the figure
# crops) is CC BY 4.0, inherited from the Starrydata dataset and from each
# figure's CC BY 4.0 source paper. Citing this work does not let you relicense
# the data under MIT.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use real-chart-bench, please cite it using the metadata in this
  file. If you use the ground-truth chart data, please also cite the
  Starrydata dataset and paper listed under `references`.
type: dataset
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
title: "real-chart-bench"
abstract: >-
  An open benchmark for chart data extraction — built from real experimental
  charts in open-access papers.
authors:
  - given-names: Tomoya
    family-names: Mato
    alias: t29mato
    email: tomoya.matou@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0918-6468"
repository-code: "https://github.com/t29mato/real-chart-bench"
version: 0.0.1
date-released: "2026-09-02"
keywords:
  - chart-data-extraction
  - benchmark
  - data-visualization
  - materials-science
  - thermoelectric-materials
  - llm-evaluation
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Starrydata: from published plots to shared materials data"
    authors:
      - given-names: Yukari
        family-names: Katsura
      - given-names: Masaya
        family-names: Kumagai
      - given-names: Tomoya
        family-names: Mato
      - given-names: Yu
        family-names: Takada
      - given-names: Yuki
        family-names: Ando
      - given-names: Erina
        family-names: Fujita
      - given-names: Fumikazu
        family-names: Hosono
      - given-names: Eiji
        family-names: Koyama
      - given-names: Farhan
        family-names: Mudasar
      - given-names: "Ton Nu Thanh"
        family-names: Phuong
      - given-names: Naoto
        family-names: Saito
      - given-names: Yoshihiro
        family-names: Sakamoto
      - given-names: Atsumi
        family-names: Tanaka
      - given-names: Dewi
        family-names: Yana
      - given-names: Kaoru
        family-names: Kimura
      - given-names: Koji
        family-names: Tsuda
      - given-names: Masahiko
        family-names: Demura
    journal: "Science and Technology of Advanced Materials: Methods"
    volume: 5
    issue: 1
    year: 2025
    doi: "10.1080/27660400.2025.2506976"
    url: "https://doi.org/10.1080/27660400.2025.2506976"
    license: "CC-BY-4.0"
    notes: >-
      Canonical paper for the Starrydata / Starrydata2 database, the source
      of this benchmark's human-digitized ground-truth XY curves.
  - type: data
    title: "20260901_starrydata2"
    authors:
      - given-names: Tomoya
        family-names: Mato
      - given-names: Masaya
        family-names: Kumagai
      - given-names: Yukari
        family-names: Katsura
    date-released: "2026-08-31"
    doi: "10.6084/m9.figshare.33399463.v1"
    url: "https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.33399463.v1"
    license: "CC-BY-4.0"
    notes: >-
      Monthly-archived snapshot of the Starrydata2 dataset on figshare
      (project "Starrydata datasets", https://figshare.com/projects/Starrydata_datasets/155129).
      The figshare project publishes a new dated snapshot on this cadence,
      each with its own DOI; this is the most recent snapshot verified at
      the time this file was written (2026-09-02). Pin to the specific
      snapshot DOI that matches the data actually ingested by this
      benchmark's collection pipeline if reproducibility of exact figures
      is required — see docs/design/benchmark-architecture.md.
